            <ArticleTitle>Prediction of significant left main coronary artery stenosis by the 12-lead electrocardiogram in patients with rest angina pectoris and the withholding of clopidogrel therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>846-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the prospective use of an electrocardiographic sign--lead aVR ST-segment elevation greater than that seen in lead V(1)--in patients with an acute coronary syndrome as a method to prompt early angiography, to withhold clopidogrel therapy, and to perform urgent coronary bypass surgery leading to successful clinical outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
